Android fd open path + embedder accessors for dspi-core (DSPi-Console-Linux core/).

Why: Android apps cannot enumerate USB with libusb (no access to
/dev/bus/usb); the app opens the device through UsbManager and hands the
usbfs file descriptor to native code. dspi-ffi wraps that fd with
`rusb::GlobalContext::open_device_with_fd` (after
`rusb::disable_device_discovery()`) and needs a way to give the resulting
handle to the core. dspi-ffi is a separate crate (UniFFI instead of the C
ABI), so it also needs public access to what lib.rs's C wrappers reach
through `pub(crate)` fields.

Choice (docs/PACKAGES.md, FFI DoD 1): three small `pub` accessors instead
of calling the core's `extern "C"` functions, so the glue stays safe Rust
and keeps the core's own types. No upstream behaviour changes; the C ABI is
untouched.

Hunks:
1. core/src/device.rs `use`: import `DeviceHandle`.
2. core/src/device.rs `DeviceManager::select_device_handle(handle, serial, vid)`
   (PLAN-NATIVE-ANDROID.md Appendix A): the tail of `select_device` for a
   handle the embedder opened. Rejects a handle whose descriptor is
   readable and not a DSPi, claims ONLY the vendor interface
   (`VENDOR_INTERFACE` = 2; never the audio interfaces 0/1; no kernel
   driver detach), starts the notify listener, records vid + serial (the
   serial is kept for auto-reconnect, as `select_device` does).
3. core/src/lib.rs `DspiCore::{device_manager, device_manager_mut,
   reset_device_state}`: public access for embedders. `reset_device_state`
   is what `dspi_select_device` did inline after a successful select.
4. core/src/lib.rs `dspi_select_device`: call `reset_device_state` (same
   behaviour, one definition).

Upstream form: identical; can be proposed to WeebLabs/DSPi-Console-Linux as is.

